00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:01.120
m 0 0 l 200 0 l 200 136 l 0 136

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:01.120
m 0 0 l 200 0 l 200 136 l 0 136

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:01.120
<b>Human (Male)
30 Years Old
(7-8 in Warrior Lv.)</b>

00:09:58.600 --> 00:10:02.100
Honor thy grandmother and grandfather!

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:06.040
Never discuss a lady's age, gao!

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:19.290
My legs!

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:22.240
Paralyze!

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:24.640
Paralyze is not paradise!

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:27.640
Oh, dear, kuma!

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:29.270
What do I do, gao?

00:10:30.770 --> 00:10:35.180
What to do... What to do, gao?!

00:10:35.770 --> 00:10:37.180
Kuma!

00:10:37.180 --> 00:10:41.040
Behold the fearsome power 
of the magibeast, bear!

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:44.560
J-Just kill me...

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:07.190
I feel like I've been through 
a serious ordeal...

00:11:07.190 --> 00:11:08.740
Oh, thank goodness!

00:11:08.740 --> 00:11:10.620
You're awake, bear?

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:13.890
I just picked you some aurange fruits.

00:11:13.890 --> 00:11:17.020
Try one. It'll perk you right up, gao.

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:18.400
Thanks...

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:21.220
This is great!

00:11:22.020 --> 00:11:24.040
Is this your house?

00:11:24.040 --> 00:11:26.400
Yes, it's my burrow.

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:27.800
Burrow?

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:30.260
I'm just so glad you're alive, bear!

00:11:30.260 --> 00:11:33.670
A hit like that really could 
have killed you, kuma.

00:11:34.120 --> 00:11:37.660
Of course, I'm the one 
that inflicted it, gao...

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:40.510
I didn't realize you were actually a woman.

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:43.410
I'm sorry for speaking so rudely.

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:46.730
I'm sorry, too, bear.

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:48.640
So, are you the one who 
nursed me back to health?

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:50.690
It wasn't me, kuma.

00:11:51.900 --> 00:11:55.260
She seems to have her own 
feelings on the subject.

00:11:55.260 --> 00:11:59.540
Carla-chan spent the entire time treating 
you with healing spells, bear.

00:11:59.540 --> 00:12:01.100
Healing spells?

00:12:02.650 --> 00:12:04.150
Is it morning already?

00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:06.790
I'd like bread for breakfast.

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:09.390
And I like my coffee with 
lots of milk and sugar,

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:12.150
and honey on my yogurt.

00:12:12.150 --> 00:12:14.130
You're a picky one, huh?

00:12:14.500 --> 00:12:17.100
And that outfit... I know what that's for!

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:24.050
<b>Picture shown for

00:12:17.090 --> 00:12:24.050
<b>Picture shown for

00:12:17.100 --> 00:12:19.160
Harattama! Kiyottama!

00:12:17.460 --> 00:12:21.170
It's for pounding nails into 
an effigy to curse someone!

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:21.160
Let this curse never be lifted!

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:27.630
You were in such awful shape, bear.

00:12:27.630 --> 00:12:29.780
The first healing spell didn't suffice,

00:12:29.780 --> 00:12:32.110
so she had to keep doing it, gao.

00:12:32.110 --> 00:12:33.900
That's a scary number of pins!

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:37.550
She called it a kind of 
magical acupuncture, gao.

00:12:37.550 --> 00:12:40.090
But you can see your wounds 
have healed, bear.

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:42.040
That's all thanks to Carla-chan, kuma!

00:12:42.040 --> 00:12:44.790
I seem all right... for now...

00:12:44.790 --> 00:12:46.070
But I'm not letting my guard down!

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:48.910
Breakfast...

00:12:50.230 --> 00:12:51.100
Hey.

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:01.600
Gracious me...

00:13:01.600 --> 00:13:04.320
She's so relieved, she's crying, bear.

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:07.280
I'morra bufeburoo...

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:08.590
You seem to be crying in 
a very self-serving way.

00:13:09.870 --> 00:13:11.730
I'm so sor—

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:13.100
I'm so sowwy.

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:14.600
Why did you change it halfway?!

00:13:14.600 --> 00:13:18.610
I did the best I could to 
cast healing spells on you.

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:20.700
But the damage was just so bad.

00:13:20.700 --> 00:13:23.390
I did manage to fix your body...

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:24.840
but your face was so unsightly...

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:26.020
Phrasing, plea—

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:26.620
Wait, my face?

00:13:27.020 --> 00:13:28.600
The wounds on your face were so bad,

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:31.610
and I, at least, wanted to get the 
general layout back to normal...

00:13:31.610 --> 00:13:32.990
<i>Did she have to reshape it?</i>

00:13:33.310 --> 00:13:36.230
I got it as close as I could 
to your original face...

00:13:36.230 --> 00:13:37.370
But it just didn't work out, and...

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:39.880
Now your face looks really stupid!

00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:42.370
Complex burn?

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:45.640
I'm afraid it's not even half-baked.

00:13:45.870 --> 00:13:48.350
Huh? Was that supposed to be a joke?

00:13:48.350 --> 00:13:49.830
You dropped your speech tic, too.

00:13:49.830 --> 00:13:52.220
Your face just looked so awful, kuma...

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:54.560
There was just nothing we could do, gao.

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:55.640
Phrasing, please!

00:13:55.640 --> 00:13:57.220
Have a look, bear.

00:13:57.570 --> 00:13:59.510
You have a hand mirror?

00:13:59.510 --> 00:14:01.720
A lady has to look her best!

00:14:01.720 --> 00:14:03.530
Magibeasts care about that?

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:05.160
But, okay...

00:14:05.160 --> 00:14:08.430
It sounds like the wounds on 
my face haven't fully healed?

00:14:08.430 --> 00:14:10.560
I'm so sowwy...

00:14:10.560 --> 00:14:12.280
You like that phrasing, huh?

00:14:12.750 --> 00:14:18.190
You said there was nothing you could do, 
but it felt perfectly fine to me...

00:14:18.190 --> 00:14:19.550
What?!

00:14:20.850 --> 00:14:23.660
Please don't hold it 
against Carla-chan, bear!

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:28.190
She worked so hard to 
restore your face, kuma...

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:29.940
But she lacked the sheer magic power...

00:14:29.940 --> 00:14:33.760
And it turned out just 
barely passable, bear...

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:37.140
Carla-chan, please don't cry!

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:43.150
I mean, I'd never even seen what Alvin-san's 
face looked like before this...

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:45.590
It's not your fault, bear.

00:14:45.590 --> 00:14:47.300
If you wish to hate someone, hate me!

00:14:47.300 --> 00:14:49.900
Hate me, a magibeast, kuma!

00:14:50.440 --> 00:14:53.780
Actually, it looks exactly 
like it always did...

00:14:54.070 --> 00:14:57.080
I'm used to being hated by your kind, kuma!

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:58.750
It's all my fault, gao!

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:00.040
No, it's my fault!

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:02.850
If only I had been stronger!

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:05.660
I'm telling you, it's back to normal!

00:15:05.660 --> 00:15:07.670
And I look pretty healthy at that!

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:16.940
I'm telling you...

00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:19.990
my face looks totally like it always did!

00:15:19.990 --> 00:15:22.440
Thank goodness! You're awake!

00:15:22.440 --> 00:15:23.870
I've <i>been</i> awake!

00:15:23.870 --> 00:15:25.620
Are you gonna pretend like 
none of that ever happened?

00:15:25.620 --> 00:15:27.760
After injuries of such severity...

00:15:27.760 --> 00:15:29.850
This is truly a miracle of God!

00:15:29.850 --> 00:15:31.990
What was all that about 
me having a stupid face?

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:34.410
Go, go, God! Viva God!

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:36.690
What was that "barely passable" stuff?

00:15:36.690 --> 00:15:39.420
And go, me, too! Viva Carla!

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:41.070
Gao!

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:46.260
I'll leave your mantle here, gao.

00:15:46.260 --> 00:15:47.290
Thanks.

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:51.310
You seem to have a lot of equipment here.

00:15:51.310 --> 00:15:55.290
Well, I was quite a wild one in my youth.

00:15:55.500 --> 00:15:59.610
I picked more than my share of fights 
with adventurers back then, bear.

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:02.600
They're a bit like trophies from 
that time in my life, gao.

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:04.920
Oh?

00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:08.370
I guess a person's personality 
changes when they get ol—

00:16:09.020 --> 00:16:11.430
Ol... Ol... Ol...

00:16:11.430 --> 00:16:15.490
Oleander, a type of tree!

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:19.240
You're such a considerate person, kuma.

00:16:20.190 --> 00:16:23.240
I think you and Carla-chan 
will get along well.

00:16:23.240 --> 00:16:25.760
I really wish I could agree with you there!

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:27.560
Give it your best, bear.

00:16:31.890 --> 00:16:33.710
<i>This feels really right.</i>

00:16:41.880 --> 00:16:44.280
In the name of God, I'll punish you!

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:47.520
Holy Beam!

00:16:50.650 --> 00:16:52.700
m 0 0 l 100 0 l 100 45 l 0 45

00:16:50.650 --> 00:16:52.700
<b>Alvin's\h
Mantle\h\h</b>

00:16:57.040 --> 00:16:59.730
You're leaving already, bear?

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:00.460
Yeah.

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:04.070
Y-You're sure you wouldn't 
like to stay longer, kuma?

00:17:04.420 --> 00:17:07.130
It feels like we were brought 
together for a reason, gao...

00:17:07.130 --> 00:17:09.220
You could always stay the night, bear.

00:17:10.000 --> 00:17:12.140
You know I can't do that.

00:17:12.140 --> 00:17:14.140
I'm a person. You're a magibeast.

00:17:14.140 --> 00:17:17.210
We didn't belong together 
in the first place!

00:17:18.490 --> 00:17:20.710
I... I suppose, gao.

00:17:21.730 --> 00:17:24.770
But I'll warn you—I'm quite a sore loser!

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:26.010
You took me by surprise this time.

00:17:26.010 --> 00:17:28.230
But next time, you won't get me so easily!

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:29.230
Bear?

00:17:29.230 --> 00:17:32.520
I'll be back for a rematch very soon!

00:17:32.520 --> 00:17:35.610
And you'd better be ready when I do!

00:17:37.100 --> 00:17:38.310
You get it?

00:17:38.310 --> 00:17:39.980
G-Gao!

00:17:42.610 --> 00:17:44.610
Ha, ha, ha, ha!

00:17:44.610 --> 00:17:47.510
Kuma! Kuma, kuma!

00:17:47.510 --> 00:17:49.760
You are quite a spirited human, gao!

00:17:49.760 --> 00:17:50.730
Very well!

00:17:50.730 --> 00:17:53.600
When you come for me, 
I'll give you quite a welcome, bear!

00:17:53.600 --> 00:17:55.640
I'll be counting on it.

00:17:55.640 --> 00:17:58.150
In the meantime, get that 
speech tic consistent!

00:17:58.150 --> 00:18:00.370
Kuma, kuma, kuma!

00:18:05.500 --> 00:18:06.770
Stop this right now!

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:09.040
You <i>bear</i>ed me, gao!

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:10.610
What is it? What's wrong?

00:18:10.870 --> 00:18:12.690
What do you think?

00:18:13.060 --> 00:18:15.600
Why... Why do you have to fight?!

00:18:16.740 --> 00:18:19.450
Why... after we'd finally become friends...

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:20.990
Now, wait a minute, kuma...

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:24.000
Why do you have to swear to fight again?

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:26.870
Seriously, read the mood...

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:26.870
Seriously, read the mood, gao...

00:18:27.180 --> 00:18:31.050
I thought we'd finally found proof that 
magibeasts and humans could get along...

00:18:31.050 --> 00:18:32.580
But we <i>do</i> get along!

00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:36.160
This is just kind of... 
a face-saving thing...

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:38.620
I really wish you'd just read the mood...

00:18:38.620 --> 00:18:41.210
Why can't you ever stop hating 
and harming each other?!

00:18:41.210 --> 00:18:42.660
It's really not like that!

00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:44.320
We really do get along!

00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:47.430
We're just pretending to be enemies, 
for appearances' sake...

00:18:47.430 --> 00:18:49.250
I'm pretty sure you're not 
supposed to explain this stuff.

00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:51.220
It feels super embarrassing...

00:18:51.220 --> 00:18:53.480
You can't fool me!

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:59.850
You were injured, and Mostly-san 
brought you all this way...

00:18:59.850 --> 00:19:04.750
She's your benefactor... 
Your <i>bear</i>nefactor!

00:19:04.750 --> 00:19:06.370
But you can't even be grateful!

00:19:07.240 --> 00:19:11.910
That said, I'm the one who 
actually healed you...

00:19:11.910 --> 00:19:15.430
So, in a way, I'm the one who 
deserves most of the credit...

00:19:16.090 --> 00:19:19.790
Not that it's all that big a deal...

00:19:19.790 --> 00:19:22.040
But I really feel like you should show

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:27.610
a little gratitude and respect to 
the person who helped you out...

00:19:27.610 --> 00:19:28.190
Bear?

00:19:28.190 --> 00:19:33.930
Of course, it's not like I picked this 
class to have people indebted to me...

00:19:34.230 --> 00:19:39.260
But if you <i>really</i> wanted to 
express your gratitude to me,

00:19:39.260 --> 00:19:43.840
I suppose I wouldn't turn you down...

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:48.700
So if you wanted to give this mace 
to me, I wouldn't turn it down.

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:51.490
I certainly wouldn't turn it down!

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:55.840
<b>Give me a reward!</b>

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:53.670
Thanks a bunch!

00:20:02.840 --> 00:20:05.110
So you just took it, huh?

00:20:05.110 --> 00:20:07.610
As compensation for my services, of course.

00:20:07.610 --> 00:20:11.110
It felt more like you fast-talked 
your way into it, to me...

00:20:11.580 --> 00:20:15.580
Anyway, how long does this 
"I die if we split up" curse last?

00:20:15.580 --> 00:20:17.600
Isn't there any way to lift it?

00:20:20.890 --> 00:20:23.080
Everything you do ticks me off!

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:25.900
Every wave! Every step!

00:20:26.900 --> 00:20:29.440
I guess we're stuck together 
for a while, then!

00:20:29.440 --> 00:20:31.590
Indeed. To my great displeasure.

00:20:31.590 --> 00:20:33.790
The displeasure is all mine, 
I can promise you that!

00:20:34.310 --> 00:20:36.070
But ah, well.

00:20:36.070 --> 00:20:40.340
You remember how I promised I'd do one 
thing you asked if you helped me?

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:41.090
Yes.

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:43.280
You saved me from my serious injuries.

00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:44.620
So I'll do what you asked.

00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:45.790
I'll form a party with you!

00:20:47.560 --> 00:20:48.690
Look after me.

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:51.800
S... Same to you.

00:20:53.630 --> 00:20:55.110
That hurt!

00:20:55.110 --> 00:20:56.820
Oh, I didn't mean...

00:20:57.820 --> 00:21:01.110
I guess you're pretty sad you didn't 
get to hold a girl's hand, though.

00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:02.540
What was that?!

00:21:02.540 --> 00:21:04.990
Yelling won't erase the 
fact that I was right!

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:10.530
Trying to prove my innocence 
is annoying, too!

00:21:10.530 --> 00:21:11.750
Tee-hee!

00:21:17.210 --> 00:21:21.130
Don't Hurt Me,

00:21:17.210 --> 00:21:21.130
Don't Hurt Me,

00:21:17.210 --> 00:21:21.130
My Healer!

00:22:27.880 --> 00:22:29.830
By the way, Alvin-hyan...

00:22:29.830 --> 00:22:31.550
What is it, <i>Carla-hyan</i>?

00:22:31.960 --> 00:22:34.160
Where are we staying tonight?

00:22:34.430 --> 00:22:38.170
It'll be morning by the 
time we reach a town.

00:22:38.170 --> 00:22:40.390
Not sure...

00:22:40.390 --> 00:22:43.430
Mostly-san offered to let us stay 
the night and everything...

00:22:43.740 --> 00:22:44.660
You...

00:22:44.660 --> 00:22:47.830
After all that posturing, 
there's no way I could've stayed the night!

00:22:48.190 --> 00:22:51.280
And it would be way too 
embarrassing to go back now...

00:22:51.930 --> 00:22:53.230
Alvin-san?

00:22:54.090 --> 00:22:55.010
What now?

00:22:55.010 --> 00:22:59.960
I'm suddenly getting a very 
keen and powerful intuition...

00:22:59.960 --> 00:23:02.100
You're actually extremely
 incompetent, aren't you?

00:23:02.940 --> 00:23:04.660
You can't even object?

00:23:05.400 --> 00:23:06.150
Bingo.

00:23:06.150 --> 00:23:07.490
You're quite sure of yourself, huh?

00:23:07.870 --> 00:23:10.990
But don't worry, Alvin-san! 
I'm with you!

00:23:12.850 --> 00:23:14.950
Just leave everything to me!

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:25.440 --> 00:23:27.000
Next episode's title is

00:23:27.840 --> 00:23:29.950
"Forced to Travel 
With Carla, a Healer,

00:23:29.950 --> 00:23:34.250
Alvin resumes his original quest 
to gather antidote herbs,

00:23:34.250 --> 00:23:36.890
but on the way he ends up attacked 
by ghosts in a graveyard

00:23:36.890 --> 00:23:39.880
which they manage to escape 
unexpectedly, but then..."

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>"Forced to travel with Carla, a healer, Alvin resumes his original
quest to gather antidote herbs, but on the way he ends up
attacked by ghosts in a graveyard which they manage to escape
unexpectedly, but then fall into a trapset by goblins and basically
the first half of the episode is filled with great suffering but Carla's
curse is still in effect so he can't get away from her and there's
even more suffering in store nevertheless and anyway these titles
are really long and kind of serve double-duty as a next episode
preview and we're pretty curious about how many people
actually listen to the whole thing and that's the deal with episode 2"</b>

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>See you then!</b>
